{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"e0f143f2-3f4d-4f15-941e-1805169a5192","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have fixed the prompt caching issue and documented the solution.\n\n### Summary of Changes\n\n1. **Split `system` prompt into two cached segments in [`bot.py`](file:///tmp/h-LTwJAH/bot.py#L130-L135)**:\n   - Updated `build_system(a, today)` to return two text blocks, each configured with `cache_control: {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}`.\n   - The first block contains the static `INSTRUCTIONS` (~780 tokens), remaining byte-identical and hot across requests and memory updates.\n   - The second block contains the dynamic `athlete_context(a, today)` tail (profile, date, zones, and facts). When `save_fact` writes a new fact, only this second segment is invalidated and re-cached (~240 tokens), rather than the entire ~1000+ token system prompt.\n\n2. **Documented in [`ANSWER.md`](file:///tmp/h-LTwJAH/ANSWER.md)**:\n   - Explained the code changes and prompt caching behavior.\n   - Noted which parts of the colleague's note applied (splitting system prompt into two ephemeral cache segments; monitoring cache metrics) and which parts were ignored (tool filtering changes, top-N fact selection, and Telegram transport details).\n","duration_seconds":43.598536,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":117291,"output_tokens":1718,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":139317,"total_tokens":119009}}}
